  "sport": "hockey",
  "title": "The arc – slalom and shot",
  "description": "All the players line up in the corner with the pucks. The first skates with the puck at high speed in an arc down towards the centre line, slaloms through the cones there and shoots as soon as their body faces the net and the puck is under control.\n\nVariation (Arc 2): the skater goes along the arc without a puck and gets a firm pass from the next in line, then shoots first time. Run it from both sides so everyone turns both ways. Works with or without a goalie. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Full speed in the arc, short puck moves in the slalom."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Turn your body towards the net before you shoot."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Variation: the passer aims where the skater is going, not where they are."
    }
  ],
